---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Install Honeybee-Revive | PH-Tools" activePage="honeybee-revive">
  <div class="content-page">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/honeybee-revive/">Honeybee-Revive</a> / Install</p>
    <h1>Install Honeybee-Revive</h1>
    <p>
      Honeybee-Revive and its Grasshopper components are free and open-source.
      The installer sets up the Grasshopper tools along with the
      <a href="https://pypi.org/project/honeybee-REVIVE/" target="_blank">Honeybee-REVIVE</a> and
      <a href="https://pypi.org/project/PH-ADORB/" target="_blank">PH-ADORB</a> Python packages.
    </p>

    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <p>Before installing, make sure you have:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.rhino3d.com/" target="_blank">Rhino-3D v8</a></li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.ladybug.tools/" target="_blank">Ladybug-Tools</a> with
        <a href="https://github.com/ladybug-tools/honeybee-core" target="_blank">Honeybee-Core</a> and
        <a href="https://github.com/ladybug-tools/honeybee-energy" target="_blank">Honeybee-Energy</a>
      </li>
      <li>Windows 10+ or macOS 13+</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout warning">
      <strong>Note:</strong> Install
      <a href="https://github.com/ladybug-tools/honeybee-core" target="_blank">Honeybee-Core</a> and
      <a href="https://github.com/ladybug-tools/honeybee-energy" target="_blank">Honeybee-Energy</a>
      before installing Honeybee-Revive.
      On Windows, use the
      <a href="https://app.pollination.cloud/cad-plugins" target="_blank">Pollination installer</a>.
      On macOS, use the
      <a href="https://www.food4rhino.com/en/app/ladybug-tools" target="_blank">Food4Rhino installer</a>.
    </div>

    <h2>Rhino / Grasshopper installation</h2>
    <p>To install Honeybee-Revive:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Install Rhino v8 if you don't have it already.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Windows:</strong> Install Ladybug Tools with the
        <a href="https://app.pollination.cloud/cad-plugins" target="_blank">Pollination Installer</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>macOS:</strong> Install Ladybug Tools with the
        <a href="https://www.food4rhino.com/en/app/ladybug-tools" target="_blank">Food4Rhino Installer</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        In Grasshopper, run the "LB Versioner" component to update Ladybug Tools to the latest release.
      </li>
      <li>
        Download the installer:
        <a href="https://github.com/PH-Tools/honeybee_REVIVE_grasshopper/releases/latest/download/hb_revive_installer.ghx" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-left: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.85rem;">Download Installer</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        Open <code>hb_revive_installer.ghx</code> in Rhino/Grasshopper and follow the on-screen prompts.
        On Windows, if you hit a permissions error, open Rhino as administrator.
      </li>
      <li>Restart Rhino and Grasshopper so the new components load.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What gets installed</h2>
    <p>The installer adds three pieces to your system:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Grasshopper UserObjects:</strong> Honeybee-Revive components (<code>.ghuser</code> files)</li>
      <li><strong>honeybee-REVIVE:</strong> core Python data model (<a href="https://pypi.org/project/honeybee-REVIVE/" target="_blank">PyPI</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>PH-ADORB:</strong> ADORB cost calculation engine (<a href="https://pypi.org/project/PH-ADORB/" target="_blank">PyPI</a>)</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Having trouble?</strong> See the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page to reach us.
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
